{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS2FQAj3mvKLWZzDyUKR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The job does run every night (6 runs, last exit code 1), but two bugs make it fail without telling you. I've written both up in `ANSWER.md` and fixed the script. I haven't run the fixed script: this folder has no repo, no `claude` login and no Telegram token. I only checked that it parses (`zsh -n`).\n\n1. **The script crashes before it can send the failure note.** In zsh, `status` is a built-in, read-only variable (it's another name for `$?`). The line `status=$?` stops the script at line 19, before either `notify.sh` call. That's why you got nothing at all, not even a failure message. You can see it in `nightly-review.err` (`read-only variable: status`) and reproduce it with `zsh -c 'status=1'`. I renamed the variable to `rc`.\n2. **`claude` isn't logged in when launchd runs it.** The error log says \"Not logged in · Please run /login\" on every run. launchd starts the script without anything from your Terminal setup (`~/.zshrc` isn't read), so the login that works when you run it by hand isn't available to the job. The script now reads a long-lived token from the keychain into `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN`, the same way `notify.sh` gets the Telegram token. If the token is missing, it sends you a failure note.\n\nI also fixed two smaller problems in `bin/nightly-review.zsh`:\n- **Failure notes now include the error.** `claude`'s error output goes to a dated `.err` file, and its first 300 characters are put in the Telegram message.\n- **The review can now read the commits.** In headless mode there's no one to approve tool use, so `git log`/`git show` would have been blocked. I allowed only read-only tools (git log/show/diff, Read, Grep, Glob), which also enforces \"do not modify any file\".\n\nTo finish on your Mac:\n1. Run `claude setup-token`.\n2. Store the token with `security add-generic-password -U -a \"$USER\" -s claude-oauth-token -w`.\n3. Copy the new script into `~/bin/`. The plist doesn't change, so it doesn't need reloading.\n4. Test it with `launchctl kickstart gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1351,"cache_read_input_tokens":25160,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1351},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a92a44a9-a44a-4766-bd33-2b7096cb166b","uuid":"d62bec14-ba25-468b-82e3-5c00820746b0","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:21:15.434Z","request_id":"req_011CgS2FPtbtFvRvNCYEtZPH"}
